{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773806670,"nonce":"oc761FTsStGbLDqUNzl4+GRSJEE=","title":"Auth requests expire too aggressively / duplicate submission not prevented","message":"Two auth requests for feature/issue-label-fix were submitted (be649609, f575b17f) and both expired before review. Two issues:\n\n1. Expiry TTL: requests should not expire while the branch is still valid and unmerged. Either extend the TTL significantly or tie expiry to branch deletion rather than wall-clock time.\n\n2. Duplicate prevention: submitting an auth request for a branch that already has a pending/expired request should update the existing record (PUT), not create a new one (POST). The second request (f575b17f) was a duplicate of be649609 with identical diff and spec.","files":null}]}